    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0329" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg217"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Rockhill</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1907-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic">February
                                16, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 253.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 499, of the 7th ultimo, in which you confirm your telegram of the
                    5th <pb facs="0330" n="218" xml:id="pg218"/> ultimo, reporting the receipt by
                    the consul-general at Canton of the sum of $25,000 gold paid by the Chinese
                    Government as indemnity for the Lienchou massacre.</p>
                <p>The dispatch has been read with interest, and your course in the matter has been
                    approved by the department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
